  "title": "Mind map: agents and processes",
  "sections": [
    {
      "h": "Centre: socialisation",
      "p": [
        "Socialisation is the process through which humans learn and internalise their culture’s norms and values, which is passed from generation to generation (Giddens, 2006). It begins from the moment of birth and extends to the point of death."
      ]
    },
    {
      "h": "Kinds of socialisation",
      "list": [
        "Primary: the family, the first stage",
        "Secondary: education, peers, the media, religion",
        "Tertiary (adult): the workplace",
        "Formal: deliberate, consciously taught",
        "Informal: unintentional, learned by watching others"
      ]
    },
